      "keyInsight": "We love to believe our minds are razor-sharp supercomputers evaluating every situation fresh. In truth, our brains are lazy energy savers that run old scripts on loop. When someone cuts you off in a sentence, an old record starts spinning automatically. You interrupt back, defend your turf, or sulk in silence without ever deciding to do so. Mindfulness sounds fancy, but it is just catching the machine while it runs. It is the tiny split second between touching a hot stove and pulling your hand back. That tiny gap is where your freedom lives. Without that pause, you are not really having a conversation at all. You are just two old tape recorders shouting pre-recorded arguments at each other across a kitchen counter.",
