      "keyInsight": "Here is a strange puzzle about everyday life. You can sit two feet away from someone on a couch and be a million miles away. You hear the sounds coming from their lips, but your mind is somewhere else. You are mentally editing an email or planning tomorrow's grocery run. This is what happens when your internal radio antenna is bent out of shape. Real communication requires a dual-band receiver. One channel tracks what is happening inside your own skin. The other channel tunes into the person sitting right in front of you. Most people tune into neither channel. They get lost in static and wonder why talks feel so lonely. Turning both dials on at the same time changes everything in seconds.",
